# Update README on changes

When you change this repository in a way that affects how people use or understand the project, update `README.md` in the same change.

## Update README when you

- Add, remove, or rename projects / top-level folders
- Change how to build, run, or configure the app (`appsettings`, CLI, dependencies)
- Add or change user-facing features (camera, PTZ, recorders, export, localization, monitors)
- Change localization workflow (new cultures, resx layout, RTL/LTR rules)
- Change external requirements (ffmpeg, SDKs, fonts, LibVLC)

## Do not churn the README for

- Pure refactors with no behavior/setup change
- Typos, formatting-only, or internal-only code moves
- Transient debug / local-only experiments

## How to update

- Keep README accurate and concise; prefer tables/lists over long prose
- Mirror real paths and commands from the repo (verify before writing)
- If localization strings or cultures change, document the files and default culture
- If a feature is removed, delete its README section instead of leaving stale text
